<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!-- =====================================================================
     PRJEDU_modbus - AyMON example 2: Modbus TCP, both ends, no hardware.

     One engine, two documents, real Modbus frames on a loopback socket
     between them:

       PLC/S00   the plant. AyMON in the SLAVE role: it listens on
                 127.0.0.1:1502, answers for unit 1 and serves four holding
                 registers that a timer keeps moving.
       MON/S00   the monitoring side. AyMON in the MASTER role: it polls
                 those registers once a second and turns them into
                 engineering values with limits and alarms.

     Read PLC/S00 first if you are putting AyMON where a device used to be,
     MON/S00 first if you are reading a device that already exists. The two
     files are the same four levels seen from opposite ends.

     A document is the unit of ownership in AyMON: separate id, separate
     log, separate lifecycle. Two of them in one process is how you develop;
     put PLC/S00 on another machine, change con_host in db_MON.xml, and
     nothing else in this example changes.

     Plain Modbus is not a licensed feature, so all of this runs on an
     unlicensed installation.

     Run:  run.bat
     ===================================================================== -->
<xdb id="XDB" xdb_lib="AyPRO" xdb_log="4" log_cfg="0x39C0" log_lnk="%PRJ%/log/XDB.log"
     sta="0x0300" tid="S01">
	<config>
		<doc id="PLC/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_PLC.xml" desc="the plant - Modbus SLAVE" />
		<doc id="MON/S00" sta="0x0300" src="%DB%/db_MON.xml" desc="the monitoring side - Modbus MASTER" />
	</config>
	<data>
	</data>
</xdb>
